 lung cancer; ADC=adenocarcinoma; BAC=bronchioloalveolar carcinoma; SCC=squamous cell carcinoma.</p></fn><fn id="t1-fn2"><label/><p>Clinical and pathological features of 114 NSCLC patients with NSCLC, classified by histological subtypes.</p></fn><fn id="t1-fn3"><label>a</label><p>Of whom eight BAC features.</p></fn><fn id="t1-fn4"><label>b</label><p>7 stages IV with unique metastasis.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">DNA sequences of primers, PNA oligomer, and probes for detecting <italic>K-Ras</italic> mutations</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Name</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>DNA (5&#x02032;&#x02013;3&#x02032;) or PNA (NH<sub>2</sub>-CONH<sub>2</sub>) sequence<sup>a</sup></bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Position,<sup>b</sup> nt</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">K-Ras F<sup>c</sup></td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">GGAGTATTTGATAGTGTATTAACCT</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">9&#x02013;33</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">K-Ras R I</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">AGAATGGTCCTGCACC</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">251&#x02013;236</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">K-Ras R II</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">GTCCTGCACCAGTAATATGC</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">244&#x02013;226</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Anchor</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">LC-Red 640-ACTACCACA AGTTTATATTCAGTCATTTTCAGCAGG-Ph</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">121&#x02013;86</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Sensor</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">CCTAC<bold><underline>GCCACC</underline></bold>AGCTC-Flu</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">138&#x02013;124</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">PNA</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">CCTAC<bold><underline>GCCACC</underline></bold>AGCTCC</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">138&#x02013;122</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="t2-fn1"><label>a</label><p>The 3&#x02032; end of the anchor probe was phosphorylated to prevent probe elongation by Taq polymerase during PCR. Underlined, nucleotide complementary to wild-type bases of codon 12 and 13.</p></fn><fn id="t2-fn2"><label>b</label><p>The base numbering is according to GenBank accession no <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="L00045" ext-link-type="gen"/>.</p></fn><fn id="t2-fn3"><label>c</label><p>F=forward; R=reverse; Flu=fluorescein; LC-Red=LightCycler-Red; Ph=phosphorylated; R I: K-Ras reverse primer used for Light-cycler analysis and classical sequencing; R II: K-Ras reverse primer used for sequencing of PNA&#x02013;PCR products.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Types of <italic>K-Ras</italic> mutations found in 114 NSCLC tumours</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>(Codon)mutation<sup>a</sup> (aminoacid change)</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Sequencing (&#x00025;)<sup>b</sup></bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Hybrisation (&#x00025;)<sup>b</sup></bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>PNA (&#x00025;)<sup>b</sup></bold></th></tr></thead><tbody 